              "name": "isol_growth_condt",
              "value": "All Mnemiopsis leidyi specimens were obtained from a single individual, 3 cm long in oral-aboral (OA) length, isolated in a 300 mL crystalizing dish with no other animals present. The offspring obtained by self-fertilization was individually pipetted to a new 300 mL culture unit, and the step was repeated every 3 days until ca. 450 animals from the same parent were isolated in 15 culture units, with ca. 30 individuals each. They were all fed extensively with Brachionus to maximize quick growth. Seven days after being transferred, only the 10 largest animals per culture unit (now ca. 3 mm in OA length) were collected in order to avoid mixing generations, as M. leidyi"
            },
